# v2.3.2330: cache headers for Cloudflare Pages.  Vite copies public/ into
# dist/ verbatim, which is where Pages reads this from; there was no _headers
# file anywhere before, so every one of the ~700 assets on a repeat load was
# revalidated -- bytes saved, round trips not.
#
# ONLY the content-hashed tree.  /assets/* filenames carry a build hash, so a
# changed file is a new URL and "immutable" can never serve a stale one.  The
# sprite and audio trees are NOT here: many of their URLs are cache-busted by a
# ?v= that the code appends, but not all of them are, and a year of immutable
# on a file that quietly changes is the "it looks fine for me" bug.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
